# Objective 2 — Tamil Nadu
#
# Policy: push everything — code, docs, images, data, ANSYS cases, MATLAB outputs and
# the archive's text — EXCEPT files git cannot take. GitHub warns above 50 MB per
# file and rejects above 100 MB, so only the oversized files (last block) are excluded.
# NOTE: later rules override earlier ones, so the size-limit block is deliberately LAST.

# ── never useful in git ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
tools/node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.asv

# ── log folders: tracked here ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The repository-wide .gitignore (one level up, shared with the other states) ignores every directory
# named logs/ AND every *.log (some OpenFOAM logs reached 285 MB). Here the logs are small and are provenance,
# so these are un-ignored: ansys/logs/ (the Fluent transcripts that used to sit loose in ansys/), results/logs/
# (the pipeline's run logs, 1 MB) and the Fluent transcripts of the seven-criteria study (~1 MB). 8 MB in all.
!ansys/logs/
!ansys/logs/**
!results/logs/
!results/logs/**
!ansys/criteria_*/fluent_terminal.log
!ansys/criteria_common/*.log

# ---- superseded work, kept on disk but mostly out of git ---------------
# archive/ is retired material: the pre-restructure implementation, the
# OpenFOAM legacy tree, superseded ANSYS cases and voided results. Nothing in
# it is live and nothing was deleted -- it stays on disk for the record.
#
# REVISED 2026-11-10. Excluding archive/ wholesale was wrong in one specific
# way: 79 of the 373 path references in the checked documents resolve ONLY
# inside archive/, so `python scripts/g12_verify_docs.py` passed on the author's
# machine and would have reported 79 missing paths on a fresh clone. Those
# references are to retired DOCUMENTS and SCRIPTS, not to the heavy data.
#
# So: archive's text content is tracked and its bulk is not (hundreds of MB --
# a 223 MB OpenFOAM run.log, CSVs, interactive HTML, JSON, the 63/81 MB
# Objective-1 aggregates). `archive/**` rather than `archive/` is deliberate:
# git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so the negations below would
# never be reached.
archive/**
!archive/**/
!archive/**/*.md
!archive/**/*.py
!archive/**/*.yaml
!archive/**/*.yml
!archive/**/*.rst
!archive/**/*.txt
# ...except the logs, which are .txt-adjacent bulk and regenerable.
archive/**/*.log
archive/**/run.log

# ADDED 2026-11-24: the DATED archive folders created when the plant changed
# (archive/<what>_YYYY-MM-DD: the legacy 2.5 m2 / 300 L/day results, the 100 L/day
# diagnostics, the old O1 inputs copy, the superseded Objective-3 contracts and the
# superseded Word reports) are small (~22 MB in all) and are tracked in FULL, so the
# previous results stay on GitHub, in archive/, exactly as they were. The heavy old
# trees (old_implementation, openfoam_legacy, ...) keep the text-only rule above.
!archive/legacy_results_300L_2p5m2_2026-11-19/**
!archive/diagnostics_100Lday_2026-11-23/**
!archive/l5_doe_partial_100Lday_2026-11-23/**
!archive/o1_inputs_copy_2026-10-29/**
!archive/superseded_obj3_contract_2026-10-27/**
!archive/superseded_obj3_contract_2026-11-09/**
!archive/superseded_reports_2026-11-11/**
# (named one by one on purpose: a date glob also matched older folders such as
#  archive/results_STALE_shifted_weather_2026-10-29, which must stay out of git)

# ── files over 50 MB (git cannot take these) — LAST so nothing above re-includes them ──
# Measured, not guessed:
#   archive/openfoam_legacy/openfoam_case/run.log   223 MB  (past the 100 MB hard reject)
#   data/objective1/suntimes.csv                     80 MB  (past the 100 MB hard reject)
#   data/objective1/daily_aggregates_tamilnadu.csv   62 MB
#   ...and the archived copies of the same two files.
# All regenerate: suntimes.csv and daily_aggregates from Objective 1's
# 00b_build_suntimes.py and 02b_build_daily_aggregates.py; run.log is solver output.
**/suntimes.csv
**/daily_aggregates_tamilnadu.csv
**/openfoam_case/run.log

# Safety net for anything that grows past the limit later.
*.pkl
